WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.296 --> 00:00:01.129
- All right, y'all.

00:00:01.129 --> 00:00:03.420
Let's wrap up with something
fun I found on social media

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.160
perfect for this particular hour.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.268
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.268 --> 00:00:08.730
(rock music)

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.640
So earlier today, we met
Lenny, the dancing doorman.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.010
You saw those skills,
you were jealous, I know.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.680
Well, just across the
pond in Dublin, Ireland

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.840
we discovered another
super talented gentleman,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.940
Sean, the singing doorman.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.550
He often greets shoppers at
a high-end department store

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.990
with a smile and tune.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.270
And he's been known to get nearby crowds

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.530
in on the music as well.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.150
We have Sean on the line right now.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.228
What's up, Sean?

00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:32.569
(audience cheering)

00:00:32.569 --> 00:00:33.600
- Hi guys, how are you?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.100
Hello from Dublin, Ireland.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.150
How are you keepin'?

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.980
- Oh my gosh, I feel like
I'm on "The Voice" again

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:38.813
with Niall.

00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:39.813
I love your accent.

00:00:40.896 --> 00:00:44.970
So, Sean, you're a doorman and a singer.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.109
Quite the talented man.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:48.150
When did you start doing that?

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.350
Just start singing?

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.350
- Well, would you believe,
Kelly, I have three jobs.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.200
I am a correctional officer.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.850
Prison officer as we call them in Ireland.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.650
I'm a singer in the evening.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.040
I sing at weddings and kind
of corporate events and so on.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.190
And then my third job, I'm
a doorman in a luxury store

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.930
called Brown Thomas in Dublin.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.880
It's a bit like
Bloomingdale's in New York.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.713
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:10.546
- If that makes sense.

00:01:10.546 --> 00:01:12.450
- So, I'm like Superman, you know,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.768
I have these different alter egos.

00:01:14.768 --> 00:01:19.768
But instead of a cape, I
have a top hat and a suit,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.130
and I transform into this
kind of singing doorman

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.247
to bring a bit of joy and
fun to the people of Dublin

00:01:26.247 --> 00:01:27.660
and Ireland in general.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.493
- I love that.

00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:30.200
So, where does the singing come in?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.010
Do you just, is it like a holiday thing

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.360
or do you do it all the time?

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.740
- Well, I've been working
with Brown Thomas,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.390
which is the store, for many, many years

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.871
and it's kind of evolved over the years.

00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:41.820
So, you kind of stand at the door,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.120
you meet and greet the
customers as a doorman,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.940
post for photos with tourists
and families and so on.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.570
But the bonus is I have a front row seat

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.430
to the amazing musicians and singers

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.410
who are busking on Grafton Street.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.660
And I sang with a guy
called Jacob Koopman.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:58.590
Lovely, lovely guy.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.350
He's one of the many very
talented buskers in Dublin.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.460
And I took my hat off like
this and I sent it around

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.190
and collected money and I
kind of tapped the money

00:02:10.045 --> 00:02:11.220
into his guitar case.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.920
And I said, "Thanks very much,
folks, back to the door."

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.780
And it went viral.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.770
It was the best fun,
you know, the best fun.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.940
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.260
- So here's the deal, okay?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.360
If you come to Dublin,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.240
look for the singing doorman,
and maybe you and I can,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.320
we can do a song together.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.295
How does that sound?

00:02:26.295 --> 00:02:27.950
- Don't you threaten me
with a good time, sir.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:28.783
(audience laughing)

00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:30.510
Yes, I love Ireland.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.470
I love Dublin.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.500
And next time I'm there,
you better sing with me.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.520
Mama's gonna show up.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.536
Don't invite her.

00:02:36.536 --> 00:02:37.560
(audience laughing)

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.970
Thank you so much, Sean.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.380
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.440
It's the first of the season,
and that's not all, my man.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.210
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.580
makers of the Frixion,
the go-to erasable pen

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:48.660
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.630
want to celebrate people
fearlessly embracing their loves

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.760
and passions and talents just like you.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.920
So they're gonna give you $1,000

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.266
How's that sound?

00:02:57.266 --> 00:02:59.258
- No.
(audience cheering)

00:02:59.258 --> 00:03:00.091
Yeah!

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.865
- Oh my gosh, Sean, I love you.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.640
I'll see you in Dublin, sir.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.569
Thank you so much.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.842
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:11.842 --> 00:03:14.719
Seth Meyers, Hoda Kotb, Jenna Bush Hager,

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:16.857
Jane Krakowski, CJ, Noelle,

00:03:16.857 --> 00:03:20.100
and everyone of you in the
audience working so hard

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.770
to spread happiness across this city.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.420
We're excited to be in New York, y'all.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.710
Thank y'all for having us.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.330
We're excited to be back on the air

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.400
and sharing daily love with all of you.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.450
Have a great day.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.467
And if it's not, try and change it.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:33.742
(audience cheering)

